KONOHAGAKURE — FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS FOR NEW RECRUITS

Q: When do I receive my forehead protector?
A: Upon passing the Academy graduation exam. It is issued by your instructor and registered to your file.

Q: How are missions ranked and paid?
A: D-rank (chores, low pay) through S-rank (extreme danger, highest pay). Genin begin with D and low C-rank missions.

Q: Who is my direct superior?
A: Your jonin-sensei leads your three-genin cell. Above them, the jonin commander and ultimately the Hokage.

Q: When can I take the Chunin Exams?
A: When your jonin-sensei nominates your full cell, typically after sufficient mission experience.

Q: What if I am injured on a mission?
A: Report to Konoha Hospital. The Medical Corps maintains your health file. Serious cases are reviewed by the Medical Corps director.

Q: Can I decline a mission?
A: Missions are assigned by rank and need. Concerns are raised through your jonin-sensei to the assignment desk.

For anything not covered here, ask your sensei or the Administration Building front desk.
